**`rust/src/lib.rs:43-47`** — added `filter_by_tag`:
```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes.iter().filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag)).collect()
}
```
Iterates in order, keeps notes where `tags` contains `tag` by exact `==` (so `foo` won't match `foobar`), preserves relative order.

**`rust/src/main.rs:33-41`** — wired `--tag <TAG>` into `list`: finds the `--tag` flag, takes the following token as the tag, and routes through `filter_by_tag` when present; otherwise lists all notes unchanged.

Verified: `cargo build` and `cargo test` (2 passed, 0 failed); manual CLI run confirmed exact-match filtering, order preservation, and empty output for an unmatched tag.

One thing to flag: `list` reads notes from `data/notes` relative to the current working directory (existing behavior), so the flag only sees whatever's in that directory.


